    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "A New Type of Toll Plaza Based on Bionics-Honeycomb"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000009",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0020-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0020-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0020-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0020-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0020-l0001",
      "p0001-n0020-l0002",
      "p0001-n0020-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "In this paper, we analyze the performance of commonly used toll plaza based on our proposed mathematical model. A new improved toll plaza is proposed to reduce the cost, decrease the probability of collision at the merging point and increase the throughput."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0021-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0021-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0021-l0000",
      "p0001-n0021-l0001",
      "p0001-n0021-l0002",
      "p0001-n0021-l0003",
      "p0001-n0021-l0004",
      "p0001-n0021-l0005",
      "p0001-n0021-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The distribution of our proposed tollbooths resembles the honeycomb. At the center of each regular hexagonal honeycomb, there are two tollbooths, which serve two separated vehicle streams. The vehicles in these two separated streams are merged in advance before they continue their journey on the highway. Due to the specific pattern of the new toll plaza, the total area can be reduced significantly. Meanwhile, the average wasted time caused by queuing can be diminished, which means that the throughput will be raised.  Additionally, by splitting the merging procedure into two stages, the possibility of accidents can also be decreased."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0022-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "The main contributions of this paper are as follows:"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0022-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0022-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0022-l0001",
      "p0001-n0022-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(1) The new designed cellular architecture can greatly reduce the construction area compared with traditional linear distributed toll gates."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0023-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(2) We analyze the throughput of toll plazas by means of the queuing theory. To verify our theory,"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0023-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0023-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0023-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0023-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0023-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0023-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0023-l0001",
      "p0001-n0023-l0002",
      "p0001-n0023-l0003",
      "p0001-n0023-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "we simulate the behavior of the large number of vehicles passing the toll plaza with the help of PTV- VISSIM. Simulation results show that the ideal cellular distributed toll booths have better results compared with traditional toll stations, especially when the traffic flow is heavy, the average travel time reduced by about 55% and the average delay time of each lane is reduced by about 70%."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0024-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0024-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0024-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0024-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0024-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0024-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0024-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0024-l0004"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0024-l0000",
      "p0001-n0024-l0001",
      "p0001-n0024-l0002",
      "p0001-n0024-l0003",
      "p0001-n0024-l0004"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(3) We analyze the influence of the proportions of different types of tollbooths to our design. According to relevant documents, the impact of exact-change tollbooths is similar to manual tollbooths, so we only consider two kinds of tollbooths: human-staffed tollbooths and E-ZPass tollbooths. PTV-VISSIM simulation results show that full ETC tollbooth is 8 times faster than full MTC tollbooth."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0025-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0025-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0025-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0025-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0025-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0025-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0025-l0000",
      "p0001-n0025-l0001",
      "p0001-n0025-l0002",
      "p0001-n0025-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(4) We simulate the performance of the cellular toll plaza under different traffic throughput. Simulation results show that the average transit time remains at about 11 seconds under different throughputs from 0 to 2000 (Unit: veh / h). We can infer that this model is not sensitive to traffic flow variations and has strong robustness which is suitable for practical construction."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0026-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0026-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0026-l0000",
      "p0001-n0026-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(5) To further reduce the possibility of accident, we improve the cellular tollbooth concept model: make the transition zone more smooth and arrange different kinds of tollbooths more equitable."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0027-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0027-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0027-l0000",
      "p0001-n0027-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "(6) For self-driving vehicles, in the center of the toll plaza, we reserve special E-ZPass tollbooths, which match the characteristics of autonomous vehicles: safer and faster."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0028-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0028-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0028-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0028-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0028-l0000",
      "p0001-n0028-l0001",
      "p0001-n0028-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Electronic toll collection and autonomous vehicles are the trends of modern transportation, our new designed model can improve the performance of toll plaza in the aspects of cost, throughput and accident prevention."
  }
]
